# Per-machine working notes. SESSION_STATUS.md has been ignored since it was
# introduced; the handoff and QA notes follow the same convention but were
# never actually covered, so a `git add -A` would have swept one in.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. These notes routinely carry production facts,
# customer names, member counts and operational detail. They belong on the
# machine that wrote them, not in the history.
SESSION_STATUS.md
/*HANDOFF*
/*QA_NOTES*
# Tracked on purpose: a 13-line tombstone pointing at SESSION_STATUS.md
# (commit 5357e92). Negated so the rule above does not read as contradicting it.
!SESSION_HANDOFF.md
